			"SHA": "73d524a3aad12fc029b5ad7373806cb4e05fcfa9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T02:17:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				142,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add IPC bridge handlers for decorations, text edits, selections, and reveal range\n\nRegister four new IPC handlers in the Sky Bridge to support extension-originated editor operations that originate in Cocoon and route through Mountain:\n\n- `sky://decoration/set-ranges`: Look up the Monaco editor matching a document URI, then apply the decoration key and ranges emitted when an extension calls `editor.setDecorations(type, ranges)`.\n- `sky://editor/apply-text-edits`: Convert extension-originated text edit payloads into Monaco `executeEdits` operations, normalizing both 0-based and 1-based range formats used by different extension code paths.\n- `sky:editor:activeChanged` / `sky:editor:selectionChanged`: Subscribe to `ICodeEditorService.onDidChangeActiveCodeEditor` and `onDidChangeCursorSelection` to push the currently active editor URI and selection state up to Mountain (and through it to Cocoon), enabling extension queries of active text editor state without polling.\n- `sky://editor/revealRange`: Accept a Monaco-1-based range and reveal type enum from Mountain and delegate to the target editor's `revealRange` API, supporting the five standard reveal strategies (Simple, Center, CenterIfOutsideViewport, NearTop, NearTopIfOutsideViewport).\n\nEach handler matches editors by full URI string or by trailing filename segment, tolerating minor URI discrepancies between extension and workbench representations. All errors are silently caught to avoid disrupting the bridge lifecycle.\n\nThis closes the gap for extensions that depend on `window.activeTextEditor` state synchronization and programmatic editor manipulation.",
			"SHA": "5db5404eb8211bf496347be688e58b5a172c0c68"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:17:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				142,
				6
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Standardize diagnostic IPC invocation formatting in Bridge\n\nRefactor all `MountainIPCInvoke` calls within the Sky Bridge initialization modules to use consistent, multi-line object formatting for the `params` array. This change affects `InstallCommands`, `InstallDeadChannelListeners`, `InstallEditorAndOutput`, `InstallFanOut`, `InstallStatusbar`, and `ProbeServices`.\n\nThis modification aligns the code style with the recent commit (caa7e63) that routed all diagnostic logs through the native IPC mechanism. By expanding the parameter objects, the error context (context ID, error objects, and specific failure messages) becomes visually distinct and easier to review, ensuring maintainability as the bridge handles increasingly complex error states.",
			"SHA": "8c98c0afaa787a8ca49f1b86f5dc1f28221929bc"
		}
	],
